# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Shell scripts MUST be LF — defense-in-depth against autocrlf=true (g-115-869).
# Without these explicit rules, `* text=auto` is heuristic-only and git's
# enforcement is not guaranteed; charlie's 2026-05-16 rc=127 incident (CRLF
# bash refusing to exec) reproduced because `_runtime.sh` was attr=text=auto,
# not attr=text eol=lf. Sibling fix: g-115-868 routes insight-trigger-sweep
# through _rt.py to bypass bash entirely.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Git hooks are shell scripts too, but EXTENSIONLESS — the *.sh/*.bash rules
# above don't match their names, so pin them to LF explicitly. autocrlf=true
# would otherwise check them out as CRLF on a fresh clone and break execution
# (same g-115-869 rc=127 class). Covers pre-commit/post-commit/pre-push and any
# future hook — critical because a fresh-clone machine (machine-2, CI) is exactly
# where the pre-push M2 tag gate must still run.
core/githooks/* text eol=lf

# Cross-machine merge self-resolution for APPEND-ONLY agent ledgers (2026-07-03,
# user-directed GitHub-sync bolstering). When the same agent identity commits
# from two machines (e.g. container alpha + desktop alpha), both sides append
# at EOF from a common base — a guaranteed textual conflict that would wedge
# iteration-push.sh's integrate step every iteration. merge=union keeps BOTH
# sides' lines (no data loss; consumers scan whole files, order-insensitive).
# SCOPE IS EVIDENCE-GATED: only files with ZERO historical deleted lines
# qualify (probe: git log -p, count '^-{' lines == 0). journal.jsonl (index
# rewrites), changelog.jsonl (pruning), experience.jsonl (archival), and
# aspirations.jsonl (RMW status updates) are NOT union-safe — a union there
# would resurrect pruned/edited lines. Their conflicts abort loudly in
# iteration-push.sh and surface for manual resolution instead.
agents/*/skill-invocations.jsonl merge=union
agents/*/health/*.jsonl merge=union
